#: ../../language/tests.md:1
msgid "Writing Tests"
msgstr "编写测试"

#: ../../language/tests.md:3
msgid ""
"Tests are important for improving quality and maintainability of a "
"program. They verify the behavior of a program and also serves as a "
"specification to avoid regressions over time."
msgstr "测试对于提高程序的质量和可维护性很重要。它们验证程序的行为，也作为规范，以避免随时间的推移出现退步。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:5
msgid "MoonBit comes with test support to make the writing easier and simpler."
msgstr "MoonBit 提供测试支持，使编写测试更加简单和容易。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:7
msgid "Test Blocks"
msgstr "测试块"

#: ../../language/tests.md:9
msgid ""
"MoonBit provides the test code block for writing inline test cases. For "
"example:"
msgstr "MoonBit 提供测试代码块，用于编写内联测试用例。例如："

#: ../../language/tests.md:11
msgid ""
"test \"test_name\" {\n"
"  assert_eq(1 + 1, 2)\n"
"  assert_eq(2 + 2, 4)\n"
"  debug_inspect([1, 2, 3], content=\"[1, 2, 3]\")\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:17
msgid ""
"A test code block is essentially a function with type `() -> Unit raise "
"Error`: it returns `Unit` and may raise an [`Error`](/language/error-"
"handling.md#error-types). It is called during the execution of `moon "
"test` and outputs a test report through the build system. The `assert_eq`"
" function is from the standard library; if the assertion fails, it prints"
" an error message and terminates the test. The string `\"test_name\"` is "
"used to identify the test case and is optional."
msgstr ""
"测试代码块本质上是一个类型为 `() -> Unit raise Error` 的函数：它返回 `Unit`，并可能抛出 "
"[`Error`](/language/error-handling.md#error-types)。它在执行 `moon test` "
"期间被调用，并通过构建系统输出测试报告。`assert_eq` 函数来自标准库；如果断言失败，它会打印错误消息并终止测试。字符串 "
"`\"test_name\"` 用于标识测试用例，是可选的。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:25
msgid ""
"Tests started by `moon test` use the module root as their current working"
" directory. Resolve relative paths used by tests from the module root, "
"rather than from the package directory or the directory containing the "
"test file."
msgstr "由 `moon test` 启动的测试以模块根目录作为当前工作目录。测试中的相对路径应从模块根目录解析，而不是从包目录或测试文件所在目录解析。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:29
msgid ""
"If a test name starts with `\"panic\"`, it indicates that the expected "
"behavior of the test is to trigger a panic, and the test will only pass "
"if the panic is triggered. For example:"
msgstr "如果测试名称以 `\"panic\"` 开头，表示测试的预期行为是触发 panic，只有在触发 panic 时测试才会通过。例如："

#: ../../language/tests.md:31
msgid ""
"test \"panic_test\" {\n"
"  let _ : Int32 = Option::None.unwrap()\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:37
msgid "Snapshot Tests"
msgstr "快照测试"

#: ../../language/tests.md:39
msgid ""
"Writing tests can be tedious when specifying the expected values. Thus, "
"MoonBit provides three kinds of snapshot tests. All of which can be "
"inserted or updated automatically using `moon test --update`."
msgstr ""
"在指定预期值时，编写测试可能会很繁琐。因此，MoonBit 提供了三种快照测试。所有这些都可以使用 `moon test --update` "
"自动插入或更新。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:42
msgid "Snapshotting `Show`"
msgstr "快照 `Show`"

#: ../../language/tests.md:44
msgid ""
"We can use `inspect(x, content=\"x\")` to inspect anything that "
"implements `Show` trait.  As we mentioned before, `Show` is a builtin "
"trait that can be derived, providing `to_string` that will print the "
"content of the data structures.  The labelled argument `content` can be "
"omitted as `moon test --update` will insert it for you:"
msgstr ""
"我们可以使用 `inspect(x, content=\"x\")` 来检查实现了 `Show` 特征的任何内容。正如我们之前提到的，`Show`"
" 是一个可以派生的内建特征，提供了 `to_string`来打印数据结构的内容。标记参数 `content` 可以省略，因为 `moon test"
" --update` 会自动插入："

#: ../../language/tests.md:48
msgid ""
"struct X {\n"
"  x : Int32\n"
"} derive(Debug)\n"
"\n"
"pub extend X with Debug::{to_repr}\n"
"\n"
"test \"show snapshot test\" {\n"
"  debug_inspect({ x: 10 }, content=\"{ x: 10 }\")\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:54
msgid "Snapshotting `JSON`"
msgstr "快照 `JSON`"

#: ../../language/tests.md:56
msgid ""
"The problem with the derived `Show` trait is that it does not perform "
"pretty printing, resulting in extremely long output."
msgstr "派生的 `Show` 特征的问题是它不能对输出进行格式化，导致输出非常长。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:58
msgid ""
"The solution is to use `@json.inspect(x, content=x)`. The benefit is that"
" the resulting content is a JSON structure, which can be more readable "
"after being formatted."
msgstr "解决方案是使用 `@json.inspect(x, content=x)`。其好处是生成的内容是一个 JSON 结构，在格式化后更易读。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:60
msgid ""
"enum Rec {\n"
"  End\n"
"  Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(Rec)\n"
"} derive(Debug, ToJson)\n"
"\n"
"pub extend Rec with Debug::{to_repr}\n"
"\n"
"pub extend Rec with ToJson::{to_json}\n"
"\n"
"test \"json snapshot test\" {\n"
"  let r = Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(\n"
"    Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(\n"
"      Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(End),\n"
"    ),\n"
"  )\n"
"  debug_inspect(\n"
"    r,\n"
"    "
"content=\"Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read(End)))\","
"\n"
"  )\n"
"  json_inspect(r, content=[\n"
"    \"Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read\",\n"
"    [\n"
"      \"Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read\",\n"
"      [\"Really_long_name_that_is_difficult_to_read\", \"End\"],\n"
"    ],\n"
"  ])\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:66
msgid ""
"One can also implement a custom `ToJson` to keep only the essential "
"information."
msgstr "也可以实现自定义 `ToJson` 来保留必要的信息。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:68
msgid "Snapshotting Anything"
msgstr "快照任何内容"

#: ../../language/tests.md:70
msgid ""
"Still, sometimes we want to not only record one data structure but the "
"output of a whole process."
msgstr "有时我们不仅要记录一个数据结构，还要记录整个过程的输出。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:72
msgid ""
"A full snapshot test can be used to record anything using "
"`@test.T::write` and `@test.T::writeln`:"
msgstr "可以使用完整的快照测试使用 `@test.T::write` 和 `@test.T::writeln` 记录任何内容："

#: ../../language/tests.md:74
msgid ""
"test \"record anything\" (t : @test.Test) {\n"
"  t.write(\"Hello, world!\")\n"
"  t.writeln(\" And hello, MoonBit!\")\n"
"  t.snapshot(filename=\"record_anything.txt\")\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:80
msgid ""
"This will create a file under `__snapshot__` of that package with the "
"given filename:"
msgstr "这将在该包的 `__snapshot__` 下创建一个具有给定文件名的文件："

#: ../../language/tests.md:82
msgid "Hello, world! And hello, MoonBit!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:85
msgid ""
"This can also be used for applications to test the generated output, "
"whether it were creating an image, a video or some custom data."
msgstr "这也可以用于测试应用程序的输出，无论是创建图像、视频还是一些自定义数据。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:87
msgid ""
"Please note that `@test.T::snapshot` should be used at the end of a test "
"block, as it always raises exception."
msgstr "请注意，`@test.T::snapshot` 应该在测试块的末尾使用，因为它总是引发异常。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:89
msgid "Property-Based Tests"
msgstr "基于性质的测试"

#: ../../language/tests.md:91
msgid ""
"Example-based tests check particular inputs. Property-based tests "
"describe a relationship that should hold for many generated inputs. Use "
"the standard library's `quickcheck` package inside an ordinary `test` "
"block; no additional module dependency is needed. For examples in a "
"`_test.mbt` file, add this import to `moon.pkg`:"
msgstr ""
"基于示例的测试检查特定输入，而基于性质的测试描述大量生成的输入都应满足的关系。在普通的 `test` 块中使用标准库的 `quickcheck` "
"包即可，无需添加额外的模块依赖。对于 `_test.mbt` 文件中的示例，在 `moon.pkg` 中添加以下导入："

#: ../../language/tests.md:97
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"moonbitlang/core/quickcheck\",\n"
"} for \"test\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:103
msgid "Checking a Property"
msgstr "检查性质"

#: ../../language/tests.md:105
msgid "Adding zero should leave an integer unchanged:"
msgstr "加零应当保持整数不变："

#: ../../language/tests.md:107
msgid ""
"test \"adding zero preserves an integer\" {\n"
"  @quickcheck.check((x : Int32) => x + 0 == x, count=100, seed=2026)\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:113
msgid ""
"Run this test with `moon test`. `check` generates inputs and calls the "
"property for each one. Returning `true` accepts a case; returning `false`"
" or raising an error causes `check` to report a failure. Here, `count` "
"requests 100 cases and `seed` makes the run repeatable. Generated `Int32`"
" values are not limited to small numbers: they can include values near "
"the limits of the type."
msgstr "使用 `moon test` 运行这个测试。`check` 会生成输入，并逐一调用性质函数。返回 `true` 表示该用例通过；返回 `false` 或抛出错误会使 `check` 报告失败。这里，`count` 指定检查 100 个用例，`seed` 使运行可以复现。生成的 `Int32` 值并不限于较小的数，也可能接近该类型的极限。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:119
msgid ""
"The input type must implement `Arbitrary` to generate values, `Shrink` to"
" simplify failing inputs, and `Debug` to display them. These "
"implementations are provided for common types, including `Int32`. Keep "
"properties deterministic and avoid mutating their inputs."
msgstr "输入类型必须实现 `Arbitrary` 来生成值、`Shrink` 来简化失败的输入，以及 `Debug` 来显示这些输入。常见类型（包括 `Int32`）已提供这些实现。性质函数应保持确定性，并避免修改输入。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:124
msgid "Understanding a Counterexample"
msgstr "理解反例"

#: ../../language/tests.md:126
msgid ""
"What about adding one? `x + 1 > x` holds for mathematical integers, but "
"does it hold for `Int32`? Small examples such as 0, 1, and 100 would all "
"pass. The following example uses `report` to look for a counterexample. "
"It returns a result instead of raising a test failure, so we can record "
"the failure report in a snapshot while keeping the demonstration itself a"
" passing test:"
msgstr "那么加一呢？`x + 1 > x` 对数学中的整数成立，但对 `Int32` 也成立吗？0、1、100 等较小的示例都会通过。下面使用 `report` 寻找反例。它返回结果而不是抛出测试失败，因此可以用快照记录失败报告，同时让演示本身保持为通过的测试："

#: ../../language/tests.md:132
msgid ""
"test \"adding one does not always increase an integer\" {\n"
"  let report = @quickcheck.report(\n"
"    (x : Int32) => x + 1 > x,\n"
"    count=100,\n"
"    seed=2026,\n"
"  )\n"
"  debug_inspect(\n"
"    report,\n"
"    content=(\n"
"      #|Falsified(\n"
"      #|  counterexample=2147483647,\n"
"      #|  tests=18,\n"
"      #|  size=17,\n"
"      #|  shrinks=0,\n"
"      #|  shrink_attempts=31,\n"
"      #|)\n"
"    ),\n"
"  )\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:138
msgid ""
"`Falsified` means the property returned `false`. The counterexample is "
"`2147483647`, the largest `Int32`. Adding one overflows and wraps to "
"`-2147483648`, so the result is smaller, not larger. This is a mistaken "
"assumption about fixed-width arithmetic, not a bug in addition."
msgstr "`Falsified` 表示性质函数返回了 `false`。反例是 `2147483647`，即最大的 `Int32`。加一会溢出并回绕到 `-2147483648`，所以结果变小了，而非变大。这是对固定宽度整数运算的错误假设，不是加法实现的缺陷。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:143
msgid ""
"QuickCheck also tries simpler inputs that still fail, a process called "
"shrinking. Here, `shrinks=0`: no smaller input preserves the failure, "
"since only the largest `Int32` fails this property. The optional "
"`max_shrinks` argument limits the number of candidates examined; "
"shrinking does not in general guarantee the smallest counterexample. Use "
"`check`, rather than `report`, when a false property should fail your "
"test suite."
msgstr "QuickCheck 还会尝试仍然导致失败的更简单输入，这个过程称为缩减（shrinking）。这里 `shrinks=0`：没有更小的输入能保留这个失败，因为只有最大的 `Int32` 不满足该性质。可选参数 `max_shrinks` 限制检查的候选输入数量；一般而言，缩减并不保证找到最小的反例。如果性质不成立时应当让测试套件失败，请使用 `check` 而不是 `report`。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:150
msgid "Keeping a Regression Test"
msgstr "保留回归测试"

#: ../../language/tests.md:152
msgid ""
"To reproduce a run, keep the seed, settings, property, and "
"toolchain/library version the same. Generated cases and shrink results "
"can change between versions. Once a counterexample reveals a bug or a "
"mistaken expectation, keep that concrete input in an example-based test "
"with the correct expected behavior:"
msgstr "要复现一次运行，需要保持种子、设置、性质函数以及工具链和库版本不变。不同版本生成的用例和缩减结果可能不同。一旦反例揭示了缺陷或错误的预期，就应将该具体输入保留在基于示例的测试中，并写明正确的预期行为："

#: ../../language/tests.md:157
msgid ""
"test \"adding one at the Int32 boundary\" {\n"
"  let x : Int32 = 2147483647\n"
"  assert_eq(x + 1, -2147483648)\n"
"  assert_eq(x.to_int64() + 1, 2147483648L)\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:163
msgid ""
"The second assertion converts to `Int64` **before** adding one, which is "
"wide enough for this calculation. Converting the result after `Int32` "
"addition would be too late: the overflow would already have happened."
msgstr "第二个断言在加一**之前**转换为 `Int64`，其范围足以容纳这次计算的结果。如果在 `Int32` 加法完成后再转换结果就太晚了：溢出已经发生。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:167
msgid ""
"Keep both kinds of tests: the regression test always checks the "
"discovered case, while the property test can explore more inputs with "
"other seeds and settings. Passing generated cases is not a proof that a "
"property holds for all inputs."
msgstr "两种测试都应保留：回归测试始终检查已发现的用例，而性质测试可以通过其他种子和设置探索更多输入。生成的用例全部通过，并不能证明性质对所有输入都成立。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:172
msgid ""
"For custom generators and more ways to choose useful properties, see "
"[Property-Based Testing in MoonBit](https://www.moonbitlang.com/blog"
"/property-based-testing-moonbit)."
msgstr ""
"关于自定义生成器及更多选择有效性质的方法，请参阅 [MoonBit "
"中基于性质的测试](https://www.moonbitlang.com/blog/property-based-testing-"
"moonbit)。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:175
msgid "BlackBox Tests and WhiteBox Tests"
msgstr "黑盒测试和白盒测试"

#: ../../language/tests.md:177
msgid ""
"When developing libraries, it is important to verify if the user can use "
"it correctly. For example, one may forget to make a type or a function "
"public. That's why MoonBit provides BlackBox tests, allowing developers "
"to have a grasp of how others are feeling."
msgstr ""
"在开发库时，验证用户是否可以正确使用它是很重要的。例如，可能会忘记使类型或函数公开。这就是为什么 MoonBit "
"提供了黑盒测试，允许开发人员了解其他人的感受。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:179
msgid ""
"A test that has access to all the members in a package is called a "
"WhiteBox tests as we can see everything. Such tests can be defined inline"
" or defined in a file whose name ends with `_wbtest.mbt`."
msgstr ""
"能够访问包中所有成员的测试称为白盒测试，因为我们可以看到一切。这样的测试可以内联定义，也可以在文件中定义，文件名以 `_wbtest.mbt` "
"结尾。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:181
msgid ""
"A test that has access only to the public members in a package is called "
"a BlackBox tests. Such tests need to be defined in a file whose name ends"
" with `_test.mbt`."
msgstr "只能访问包中公开成员的测试称为黑盒测试。这样的测试需要在文件中定义，文件名以 `_test.mbt` 结尾。"

#: ../../language/tests.md:183
msgid ""
"The WhiteBox test files (`_wbtest.mbt`) imports the packages defined in "
"the `import` and `wbtest-import` sections of the package configuration "
"(`moon.pkg`, or legacy `moon.pkg.json`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../language/tests.md:185
msgid ""
"The BlackBox test files (`_test.mbt`) imports the current package and the"
" packages defined in the `import` and `test-import` sections of the "
"package configuration (`moon.pkg`, or legacy `moon.pkg.json`)."
msgstr ""
